// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - MindFreedomSouvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3741901036" "Seer 1381's Mask"
// tDetailString :
"P2036519514" "Katie Douglas no longer needed her Seer mask where she was headed. So you picked it up as a memento to remind yourself that those who are free don't seem to:<br><br><b><color paragon>Mind Freedom</color></b><br><br>Katie Douglas had been a Seer for half of her life. She had vowed to free the other Seers so that they would no longer be slaves to the people of Praetoria. It was at the Seer Subnet Facility where you were faced with a choice: Let Katie release the Seers from the Network but in the process cripple the PPD, giving the Syndicate and Destroyers free reign over the city, or stop Katie Douglas and keep the city safe, but validate the idea that just because you are born different it is okay to be enslaved."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Marchand 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro1 Text :
"P1707472761" "What in Cole's blue eyes is going on?!<br><br>I've got reports of a raid into the B.A.F., a prisoner escape, numerous T.E.S.T. teams and Seers injured or killed.<br><br>And worst. Tilman is breathing down my neck about Seer 0001 winding up dead.<br><br>When I said 1 Seer is worth the risk, I meant the one you were helping, not one of Tilman's favorite <i>pets</i>!"
// Answer Text :
"P2978944241" "I was following your orders, sir."
// Page Intro2 Text :
"P1270337533" "What in Cole's blue eyes is going on?!<br><br>I've got reports of a raid into the B.A.F., a prisoner escape, numerous T.E.S.T. teams and Seers injured or killed.<br><br>And worst. Tilman is breathing down my neck about Seer 0001 winding up dead.<br><br>What are you doing?"
// Answer Text :
"P1565764992" "I'm helping a Seer, I believe she'll lead us to the Resistance."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P68570982" "<color orange>Marchand grumbles his displeasure</color><br><br>Whatever she is planning next, if it is going to cause further damage to the Seer program, stop her. But if it looks like she might lead us to Calvin Scott or another high priority target in the Resistance echelons, then you let her do as she pleases.<br><br>You understand?"
// Answer Text :
"P2879491772" "She's planning on deactivating a Seer subnet facility."
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P943732335" "If she threatens more of Tilman's <i>pets</i>, then stop her. If not, then I don't care either way."
// Answer Text :
"P4262229902" "Understood."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Seer1381DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1474574621" "My mother wanted me to be free, {HeroName}, but why should I be the only one? I'm going to free the others, let them live their lives how they see fit."
// Answer Text :
"P4126636940" "Let's go!"
// Answer Text :
"P337172684" "I'm not ready yet."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Mayhem 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3041139598" "{HeroName}. Don't you recognize me? I am <color yellow>Mother</color>, or, if you prefer, <color yellow>Praetor Tilman</color> is fine.<br><br>I'm afraid our conversation cannot be more <i>pleasant</i> given the circumstances, but I see you've handled the nasty little issue with one of my dear <i>daughters</i> here. Really, I <i>must</i> apologize for the mess she pulled you into. I think we can both agree that my little Seers can be <i>such</i> troublemakers when they aren't <i>properly</i> supervised. <br><br>Let it be no more bother to you, {HeroName}, Mother is here, so you won't need to deal with this any further. I'll make sure my girl is kept in line and made to understand the importance of doing as she is told. As for you, I'll make sure you are well rewarded."
// Answer Text :
"P3799730406" "I didn't do this for you, Tilman. I know what you do to these women."
// Answer Text :
"P191013611" "Anything to serve the empire, Mother."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P924276879" "<color orange>Praetor Tilman's sly smile curves downward dangerously.</color><br><br>I don't think I like your tone, little {Hero.gender=male man|miss}!<br><br>Do you <i>truly</i> understand, what I <i>do</i>?<br><br>I am the Seers. They cannot exist without my guidance. And without them, Praetoria would spiral into chaos.<br><br><color orange>Praetor Tilman seethes for a moment and then tucks a strand of purple hair behind her hair and composes herself.</color><br><br>I apologize, {HeroName}, I'm sure you didn't mean to upset me so. I simply get <i>agitated</i> when people insinuate that I would <i>ever</i> seek to harm one of my girls."
// Answer Text :
"P3956083999" "Maybe not today, Tilman. But one day, I'll make sure you pay for your crimes. I promise."
// Page NotToday Text :
"P433901610" "<color orange>Praetor Tilman maintains her aloof composure, letting your words wash over her with a smirk.</color>I see. Well I'll be looking forward to that day then, {HeroName}.<br><br><color orange>Tilman's eyes narrow into thin slits and she scowls</color><br><br>But until that day, remember this. <i>Mother</i> is watching you."
// Answer Text :
"P2385719541" "(Leave)"
// Page PageFinish Text :
"P3575237424" "Such a good, loyal {Hero.gender=male man|woman}! It's inspiring. But you really shouldn't be bothered with the petty antics of my little girls. I'll... clean up the mess around here and remind my daughters, <i>again</i>, that it isn't nice to waste other people's time."
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P999956926" "My mother was trying to tell me that time is precious, and that we never know when it's going to run out or be taken from us.<br><br>{HeroName}, I sacrificed half my life just because I was born different from other people. Every Seer in this city is forced to do the same. Help me put an end to this madness!"
// AcceptString :
"P74220263" "Help Katie Douglas"
// SendOffString :
"P660473208" "There's a Seer subnet facility not far from here. I'll teleport us there when you are ready.<br><br>Nobody should have to suffer for the benefit of others. <br><br><color yellow>Those Loyalists who are <i>truly</i> loyal to the safety and peace of Praetoria would do well to speak with Provost Marchand about events that are happening.</color>"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1713086359" "Deactivate Seer Subnet (Single Player)"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1268672163" "When you are ready to go, I will take you."
// TaskTitle :
"P147733305" "<color deepskyblue>Mind Freedom</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P543589868" "<color deepskyblue>Freedom for All</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2426637539" "This facility resonates psychic power. If they didn't see you coming before, they certainly are aware of you now."

